// fuai_caps.lomt — FUAI's three index spaces as Loment capability domains.
//
// The language's `capability` + `guard` is an index-space declaration, not an
// authorization mechanism: a guard traps on a literal out-of-range index at
// compile time and increments the guard audit table for a runtime index. The
// authorization itself stays where the contract puts it — `cap_exec` and the
// capability table in fuai_core.
//
// These three declarations give the checker the shapes the C reference only
// documents:
//   slots   0..7   capability slots (fuai_cap_grant / fuai_cap_check)
//   domains 0..4   0 = system domain, 1..4 = revocable domains
//   actions 1..7   the exec action bits (1 = KILL ... 7 = BOX_CMD)
//
// Every guard in fuai_core is placed AFTER the dynamic check, so the FUAI
// contract (out-of-range returns -22, unauthorized returns -1) is unchanged;
// what the language adds is the compile-time rejection of a literal that can
// never be valid (E004).

module fuai_caps

choose runtime

capability fuai_slots : slot[0..7] revocable
capability fuai_domains : domain[0..4] revocable
capability fuai_actions : act[1..7] revocable
